        "explanation": "Key architectural principles of **Database Connection URLs, Credentials, and Properties**:\n1. **Weak Generational Hypothesis:** The vast majority of created objects die shortly after allocation; memory is partitioned into Young Gen (Eden, S0, S1) and Old/Tenured Gen.\n2. **Minor GC vs Full GC:** Minor GC collects dead objects in Eden rapidly with small pauses; surviving instances promote to Old Gen after passing age thresholds.\n3. **Regional Compaction (G1 GC):** G1 divides the heap into uniform 1MB-32MB regions, prioritizing collection of regions with the highest ratio of dead objects.\n4. **Concurrent Collectors (ZGC):** Uses colored pointers and load barriers to mark and relocate live objects concurrently with application threads, achieving sub-millisecond pause times.",
        "importantConcepts": [
          "G1 GC is the default collector in Java 17 LTS (-XX:+UseG1GC).",
          "ZGC provides predictable sub-millisecond pauses on heaps from megabytes to terabytes.",
          "Metaspace stores loaded class metadata in native memory outside the Java heap.",
          "Avoid explicit System.gc() calls as they force unoptimized full stop-the-world pauses."
        ],
