        "explanation": "Core mechanics of **Why Optional Must Never Be Used for Method Parameters or Fields**:\n1. **Pipeline Architecture:** A Stream pipeline consists of a Source (Collection, array), zero or more Intermediate operations, and exactly one Terminal operation.\n2. **Lazy Evaluation:** Intermediate operations (`filter`, `map`, `sorted`) are not executed immediately; they form an execution recipe evaluated only when a terminal operation is called.\n3. **Short-Circuiting:** Operations like `findFirst()`, `anyMatch()`, and `limit()` terminate processing as soon as a condition is satisfied without iterating the entire dataset.\n4. **Immutability:** Streams do not alter the underlying data source; they yield new values or collect into new immutable data structures.",
        "importantConcepts": [
          "Intermediate operations return a new Stream and are always lazy.",
          "Terminal operations (collect, reduce, count, forEach) trigger pipeline execution and consume the stream.",
          "A Stream cannot be reused once a terminal operation has executed.",
          "Optional<T> prevents NullPointerExceptions by modeling the presence or absence of a value."
        ],
